# Backend selection for FencingManualTranslator model serving.
# Copy to backend.env and edit. Changing values + `docker compose up -d`
# recreates the container with the new settings -- NO image rebuild
# (both local backends are baked into the image).
#
# backend.env is gitignored (it can hold REMOTE_API_KEY).
# Keep KEY=value lines clean -- no trailing inline comments (compose's
# env_file parser is picky about them across versions).

# local | remote
BACKEND_MODE=local

# ---------- BACKEND_MODE=local ----------
# Which prebuilt llama.cpp backend the container runs:
#   vulkan   - mesa RADV via the LunarG SDK (default, most portable)
#   rocm7    - ROCm 7.2.4 stable HIP build
#   rocm714  - ROCm 7.14 preview (NOT built yet; selecting it fails
#              -- see docker/ROCM714_NOTES.md)
LLAMA_BACKEND=vulkan

# ---------- BACKEND_MODE=remote ----------
# Point the pipeline at a llama-server (or llama-swap) on another LAN
# machine. This host then needs no GPU -- run `scripts/setup.sh --remote`,
# which also drops in docker-compose.override.yml. Full setup + the
# Windows GPU-system side: docs/remote-gpu.md.
#
# REMOTE_HOST: the GPU system's LAN IP -- give it a DHCP reservation.
REMOTE_HOST=
REMOTE_PORT=11500
REMOTE_API_KEY=
#
# Model routing. With llama-swap on the GPU system, the pipeline sends these
# as the request "model" field and llama-swap swaps the vision/text model
# automatically -- set them to your llama-swap map keys. With a bare
# llama-server, leave them and swap the model by hand between step 1 and 2.
VLM_MODEL_NAME=fmt-ocr
TRANSLATION_MODEL_NAME=fmt-translate

# --- Display ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The time zone scripts/progress.sh shows times in ("14:39 Eastern (18:39
# UTC)"). The systems and logs keep UTC. A tz database name, e.g.
# America/New_York, Europe/Paris; empty = UTC only. DISPLAY_TZ_LABEL names it
# on screen (default: the zone's abbreviation, EDT / EST).
DISPLAY_TZ=
DISPLAY_TZ_LABEL=
